# Styling and UI Standards

## CSS Approach

- Use Tailwind CSS for utility-first styling
- Use CSS Modules for component-specific styles when needed
- Prefer composition over custom CSS

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Tailwind utilities
export function BookingCard({ booking }: BookingCardProps) {
  return (
    <div className="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
      <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
        {booking.customerName}
      </h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">
        {formatDateTime(booking.dateTime)}
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Component Library

- Use consistent design system
- Create reusable UI components (Button, Input, Card, etc.)
- Maintain consistent spacing and typography

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Reusable button component
interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
}

export function Button({ 
  variant = 'primary', 
  size = 'md', 
  className,
  ...props 
}: ButtonProps) {
  const baseStyles = 'font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors';
  const variants = {
    primary: 'bg-blue-600 text-white hover:bg-blue-700',
    secondary: 'bg-gray-200 text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-300',
    danger: 'bg-red-600 text-white hover:bg-red-700',
  };
  const sizes = {
    sm: 'px-3 py-1.5 text-sm',
    md: 'px-4 py-2 text-base',
    lg: 'px-6 py-3 text-lg',
  };
  
  return (
    <button
      className={cn(baseStyles, variants[variant], sizes[size], className)}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}
```

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML
- Include ARIA labels where needed
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper color contrast

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Accessible form
<form aria-label="Formulario de reserva">
  <label htmlFor="customerName" className="block text-sm font-medium">
    Nombre del Cliente
  </label>
  <input
    id="customerName"
    type="text"
    required
    aria-required="true"
    className="mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-gray-300"
  />
</form>
```

## Responsive Design

- Mobile-first approach
- Test on multiple screen sizes
- Use responsive Tailwind classes

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Responsive layout
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {bookings.map(booking => (
    <BookingCard key={booking.id} booking={booking} />
  ))}
</div>
```
